{{General Punctuation character info|hex=2019|name=RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK}}
==Translingual==

===Alternative forms===
* [[']]
* {{sense|transliterated Cyrillic}} [[′]]

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=mul}}

===Symbol===
{{head|mul|symbol}}

# End of a [[quotation]].
# {{context| in [[transliterate]]d [[Cyrillic]] text|lang=mul}} Transliteration of the [[soft sign]] ([[ь]]), indicating [[palatalization]] of preceding consonants.
# {{context| in [[transliterate]]d [[Arabic]] and [[Hebrew]] text|lang=mul}} Transliteration of the [[glottal stop]] ([[hamza]]).
# A [[glottal stop]] in the orthography of numerous languages of America, Africa, and formally the Pacific. In most [[Polynesian]] languages, the convention has shifted to the [[okina]] <[[ʻ]]>.
# {{context|informal|lang=mul}} A substitute for the diacritic [[ʼ]] used in the [[International Phonetic Alphabet]] for [[ejective]] and other glottalized consonants.

